{
  "_note": "GRAMMAR A0, the founding principle: show as was, not as is, and never tell. The one list both sides read: studio/engine/aswas.py (the engine's plan-time lints on narration, cards, lower thirds and overlays) and scripts/lib/show-as-was.mjs (films.json copy, the page templates and the generated meta descriptions). Matching: words are matched whole and case-insensitively, a space or hyphen in a phrase matches any run of spaces or hyphens, and text inside double quotes (straight or curly) is skipped, because quoted period speech is exempt, and a group's except phrases are blanked before its phrases are matched. Period names are matched whole and case-sensitively, refused only while the film's horizon (as_of) is before the date the modern form came into use (until); a phrase in except is period-correct and never refused. Adding a phrase needs a test in tests/fixtures/a0-cases.json, which both suites read.",
  "version": 1,
